    "ruleType": "unit-ability",
    "group": "Commissar Yarrick",
    "summary": "As [your opponent's Movement phase](vsdata:core-rule/movement-phase) ends, you can pick an enemy unit that ended a move, or was set up, up to 8\" from this model, and a **REGIMENT** unit of yours that is [visible](vsdata:core-rule/visibility) to this model, up to 6\" from it, and has neither made a [Normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move) nor been the target of the **[Fire Overwatch](vsdata:ability/core.fire-overwatch)** Stratagem in the phase. The picked **REGIMENT** unit can then do one of these:\n\n- move up to D6\" with a [Normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move)\n- shoot, but only at the picked enemy unit, and only if that unit is an eligible target; each of its ranged attacks hits only if its [Hit roll](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls) is an unmodified 6, whatever its weapon's BS or any modifiers, for the rest of the phase\n- declare a charge; its [charge move](vsdata:core-rule/charge-move) has to end **engaged** with the picked enemy unit, and even a successful charge gives it no Charge bonus that turn",
